.TH fleetring-router 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-router \- Runs a router, the libSQL/Hrana front door to the fleet
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring router\fR [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-config\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a router, the libSQL/Hrana front door to the fleet.
.PP
Serves Hrana over HTTP (`/db/<database>/v3/pipeline`), so that unchanged libSQL and Turso
clients reach each database\*(Aqs primary. Every request carries a FleetRing token as its
`authToken`; the router verifies it, checks read on the database, and forwards it to the node.
The router connects to the fleet with its own client certificate, for a principal every node
lists with `forward_tokens = true`.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
The router\*(Aqs TOML configuration file
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
